---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import AsideNav from '../../components/AsideNav.astro';
const path = '/data-sanitization/standards';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Data Sanitization', href: '/data-sanitization' },
  { name: 'Standards', href: path },
];
---
<Base
  title="Data Sanitization Standards: NIST SP 800-88, NSA/CSS 9-12 and NSA EPL"
  description="The standards behind secure data destruction: NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1 Guidelines for Media Sanitization, the NSA/CSS Policy Manual 9-12 and the NSA Evaluated Products List."
  path={path}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero crumbs={crumbs} eyebrow="Standards" title="Data Sanitization Standards" lead="The international standards and guidelines our processes follow." />
  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap with-aside">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">The need for standards</h2>
        <p>
          Without a set of standards, what people consider "destroyed", or how they think data is protected, would differ widely
          from what is actually needed to ensure complete destruction. Standards, and devices that meet them, mean that data needing
          protection is disposed of properly. That ranges from your own personally identifiable information (PII) to national and
          military secrets that protect millions of lives.
        </p>

        <h2>US National Institute of Standards and Technology, NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1</h2>
        <p>
          NIST Special Publication 800-88 Revision 1, Guidelines for Media Sanitization, is the current internationally recognized
          standard for organizations and agencies sanitizing data and storage media that leave their control.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-88r1.pdf" rel="noopener">Read NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1 (PDF)</a></p>

        <h2>NSA/CSS Policy Manual 9-12</h2>
        <p>
          The NSA/CSS Policy Manual 9-12, Storage Device Sanitization and Destruction Manual, gives routine guidance for sanitizing
          information system storage devices for disposal or recycling, in line with DoD Manual 5200.01 Volume 3, Intelligence
          Community Standard 500-34 (Electronic Waste Management and Disposal) and NSA/CSS Policy 9-12. Information on these devices
          may range from UNCLASSIFIED to TOP SECRET. The manual also explains how to obtain current listings of evaluated
          sanitization equipment that meets NSA/CSS specifications.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://www.nsa.gov/Resources/Media-Destruction-Guidance/" rel="noopener">NSA media destruction guidance</a></p>

        <h2>National Security Agency Evaluated Products List (EPL)</h2>
        <p>
          The NSA/CSS Evaluated Products List is a continually updated list of products proven to destroy data beyond recovery. Our
          <a href="/data-sanitization/equipment">degausser and HDD crusher</a> are NSA/CSS-evaluated models.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://www.nsa.gov/Resources/Media-Destruction-Guidance/NSA-Evaluated-Products-Lists-EPLs/" rel="noopener">NSA Evaluated Products Lists</a></p>
      </article>
      <AsideNav section="/data-sanitization" path={path} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
